WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.155
The Boy Who Cried Wolf

00:00:02.855 --> 00:00:08.816
There once was a shepherd boy who was bored as he sat on the hillside watching the village sheep.

00:00:09.466 --> 00:00:18.468
It was rather lonely for him all day, so he played on his shepherd's pipe, and thought upon a plan by which he could get a little company and some excitement.

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:22.831
To amuse himself he took a great breath and sang out, "Wolf!

00:00:23.181 --> 00:00:25.051
The wolf is chasing the sheep!"

00:00:25.701 --> 00:00:30.139
The villagers came running up the hill to help the boy drive the wolf away.

00:00:30.489 --> 00:00:34.009
But when they arrived at the top of the hill, they found no wolf.

00:00:34.659 --> 00:00:37.542
The boy laughed at the sight of their angry faces.

00:00:37.892 --> 00:00:44.832
"Don't cry 'wolf', shepherd boy," said the villagers, "when there's no wolf!" They went grumbling back down the hill.

00:00:45.482 --> 00:00:48.483
The boy felt a little ashamed, but not for long.

00:00:48.833 --> 00:00:52.920
For the joke had been such fun, he could think of nothing else all day.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.065
Later, the boy sang out again, "Wolf!

00:00:56.415 --> 00:01:04.129
The wolf is chasing the sheep!" To his naughty delight, he watched the villagers run up the hill to help him drive the wolf away.

00:01:04.778 --> 00:01:11.242
When the villagers saw no wolf they sternly said, "Save your frightened song for when there is really something wrong!

00:01:11.592 --> 00:01:18.496
Don't cry 'wolf' when there is NO wolf!" But the boy just grinned and watched them go grumbling down the hill once more.

00:01:19.146 --> 00:01:23.309
That evening the boy promised himself he would never play the trick again.

00:01:23.659 --> 00:01:26.808
But a promise made to yourself is easy to forget.

00:01:27.458 --> 00:01:32.630
Later, he saw a REAL wolf prowling about his flock, come out from the dark forest.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:37.920
Alarmed, he leaped to his feet and sang out as loudly as he could, "Wolf!

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:39.145
Wolf!"

00:01:39.795 --> 00:01:44.085
But the villagers thought he was trying to fool them again, and so they didn't come.

00:01:44.435 --> 00:01:48.377
"He cannot fool us again," they said, and went on with their work.

00:01:49.027 --> 00:01:54.732
At sunset, everyone wondered why the shepherd boy hadn't returned to the village with their sheep.

00:01:55.082 --> 00:01:57.176
They went up the hill to find the boy.

00:01:57.826 --> 00:01:59.333
They found him weeping.

00:01:59.683 --> 00:02:01.426
"There really was a wolf here!

00:02:01.776 --> 00:02:03.241
The flock has scattered!

00:02:03.591 --> 00:02:06.094
I cried out, 'Wolf!' Why didn't you come?"

00:02:06.744 --> 00:02:10.819
An old man tried to comfort the boy as they walked back to the village.

00:02:11.169 --> 00:02:22.486
"We'll help you look for the lost sheep in the morning," he said, putting his arm around the youth, "Nobody believes a liar, even when he is telling the truth!" And that is the end of the tale.

